f 1074 "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x-h)}{2h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=3$ with the step size $h=0.1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ≈\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x-h)}{2h} \\\\ {f}^{′}(3) & ≈\\frac{f(3+0.1)-f(3-0.1)}{2(0.1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(3.1)-f(2.9)}{0.2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7.11-5.91}{0.2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1.2}{0.2} \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296148 #edb/ref 1080 "-0.5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296148 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296148 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a7e2085a-e531-5baf-8fe5-1d1d7a6ad9e4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296904 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186296148 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296904 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296904 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296904 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186296148 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296904 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "8369a49e-b4e6-517f-b327-76c2f9620e9c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297414 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186296904 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297414 #edb/ref 1069 "q-314898" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297414 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297414 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/d2/d27b0d70171683240fd44c8bbbcc8cb46ce0f0f216533a8061d31a991cce4e14.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Approximate ${f}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=2$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=1.$\n\n*Hint: Assume that the graph passes through the points with integer $y$-coordinates when $x=1$ and $x=3.$*\n\n${f}^{′}(2)≈$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297414 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4894e4a4-bc69-5cbe-8eef-c136c4c17945" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297414 #edb/ref 1074 "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x-h)}{2h},\n$$\n\nat the point $x=2$ with step size 